# Byte-exact checkout, everywhere. Do not remove.
#
# faultattr/norms/*.md are sha256-pinned in the matching *.lock.json, and
# verify_norms() aborts every experiment if one of those hashes moves. Git's
# default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which changes those bytes and therefore those hashes: magentic_one.md goes
# from dab067b8... to d0af8b6e... and nothing will run. The per-case hashes in
# the Who&When download record depend on byte-exactness in the same way.
#
# So: no end-of-line conversion for any path in this repository.
* -text
